Qwen3.8-Flash-Next vision patch 01: vision tower on the first rank, streamed from host.

vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/model.py

Needs flash-next-mem-01-pp-embed-head.patch for the memory it frees.

Without --language-model-only the vision tower (27 blocks, 0.836 GiB BF16) was
built on every pipeline rank, although vLLM runs the encoder on the first rank
only. It is now built there only.

The tower is built and loaded on the host and moved to the GPU by
process_weights_after_loading(), after the MoE repacks have run: the first
rank has no room for it on top of their load-time transients.

With VLLM_VISION_HOST_STREAM=1 (the default) only the patch embedding, the
position embedding and the merger go to the GPU. The 27 blocks stay in pinned
host memory, and each block is copied into one of two GPU slots (58 MiB) just
before it runs, the next one on a side stream while the current one computes.
A block's weights take 1.16 ms to cross PCIe 4.0 x16 (26 GB/s); computing it
takes about 4 ms for a 1 MP image, so only the first copy shows: the tower
takes 111.7 ms instead of 109.5 ms for a 1 MP image and 295.5 instead of
293.1 ms for 2 MP. Below ~0.4 MP the copies dominate, at most ~12 ms per image.

On 3 x RTX 3090 this keeps the text-only KV cache (262,144 x 4) with vision
on. VLLM_VISION_HOST_STREAM=0 keeps the whole tower on the GPU instead, which
then needs --kv-cache-memory-bytes lowered to about 480000000 (262,144 x 2.44).

